"""Production AlexNet backend for the genuine partition-free Option-A runtime.

This module deliberately contains no layer/partition walker.  It resolves the
registered executable, measures a whole-axis exact conserving raw target-logit
positive-removal field into the rank-eight CUDA Frequent-Directions producer,
identifies a current-mask layer-feature correction, and declares a small finite
set of complete packed global actions.  Every accepted action invalidates that
geometry: the backend then repeats the measurement, correction, and global
ordering at the exact new mask before another candidate can be frozen.

The historical v0 mask is comparison/calibration metadata only.  It is never a
v1 finite action and never contributes a route to the v1 ordering.  A separately
sealed comparator retained-count may add only the exact cardinality checkpoint
when the ordinary v1 ladder would already cross it; it cannot enlarge a natural
step, and it disappears after that scalar checkpoint is reached.  Each
current-mask chart scores the complete live singleton field
and declares a compact finite backtracking ladder of global packed masks ranked
by the corrected singleton surrogate.  Those masks are proposal candidates
only: acceptance is always decided by exact proposed-mask-minus-dense BCE
evidence under the registered dense-relative budget.  Layer identities supply
correction features for legally removable layers and nonempty-layer legality
only; they never create layer queues, budgets, or traversal partitions.

Terminal rows are structurally isolated in a callable that is invoked only by
the production terminal firewall.  Its first invocation evaluates the dense
and frozen terminal masks on one common, predeclared panel and exposes a typed
trajectory observation.  Calling its observation method before that reveal
refuses.

Artifact preparation contract
-----------------------------
The twelve files admitted by :mod:`modern_v1_alexnet` are themselves immutable.
The two context-bank JSON files may bind large external bank replicas by an
absolute path plus SHA-256.  The extraction-calibration JSON owns only the v1
decision calibration, dynamic removal fractions, independent retained-route
floor, dense-relative proposed-mask damage guard, correction context IDs, and
required atomically supplied `tau_F`/`tau_Q` selector-budget identities.  The
historical v0 mask and receipt are absent from that extraction binding; they
may appear only in separate comparison provenance and as the terminal
comparison-calibration anchor.  Calibration slope transports the registered
calibrated-logit trust radii analytically into raw-logit units; sigmoid/BCE
pullbacks remain exclusive to the direct acceptance oracle.  Every referenced file is rehashed before model
construction.  Paths never supply scientific defaults: all identities,
context IDs, calibration values, action fractions, and runtime coordinates are
explicit in the sealed JSON.

This remains an internal development backend.  Its receipts are evidence, not
selector promotion or a scientific superiority claim.
"""

